 "customerTurns": 5,
 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "microwave not working"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "I can help you troubleshoot this. When a microwave appears 'not working', it usually means either there is no power at all (no lights on the display), or it powers up but refuses to start cooking. To narrow this down quickly:\n1. Check that the plug is secure and the wall socket has power (you can test with a lamp).\n2. Look at the display: is it completely blank, or are there lights/symbols showing?\n3. If you see symbols but nothing happens when you press Start, check if a 'Lock' or key symbol is lit; holding 'Stop' for 3-5 seconds often cancels this. Please let me know what the display shows and whether the socket seems to have power."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "display is on, shows the time. theres a little L symbol too. door light comes on when i open it"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "That 'L' symbol usually means the control lock (child safety) is on, which stops the buttons from working. To turn it off: hold down the 'Stop' or 'Cancel' button for about 3 to 5 seconds until you hear a beep and the 'L' disappears. Does that work?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "ok trying it now"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Let me know if that worked. Did the 'L' go away and did you hear a beep? If it has, please put a mug of water inside and press Start for one minute to see if it heats up."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "yes the L has gone and it beeped. trying the water now"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Good news on the lock clearing. Please let me know if the water has heated up in that minute. If it is hot, your microwave was just locked and is working fine now. If it is still cold (but you hear it running), there may be an internal fault like a door switch or magnetron issue."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "yep it works, the water's hot. thanks"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "That's excellent news. It was just the control lock preventing it from starting. To avoid this happening again by accident, remember that holding 'Stop' for a few seconds is how you toggle that feature on and off. Is there anything else I can help you with today?"
  }
 ],
